According to the default naming convention, ASP.NET Core searches in this
folder for the controllers of our app.
Properties/launchSettings.json file represents the settings for our project.
This file is created when you try to change any of your project's properties, and it
usually stores the application URL for our services or apps. Furthermore, if we
have a quick look at the content of the file we can notice two different profiles:
one with the name of the project created, and another one with the IISExpress
