Partial updating
Put actions are used to replace a resource with another one. Therefore, the client must add
the whole entity in the body payload of the request. If our entity is a complex object, keeping
the entire entity in memory may cause performance issues. It is possible to avoid these
problems by implementing a Patch action instead. The Patch action usually modifies an
existing resource without replacing it, therefore you are able to specify only one the field
you want to update. Let's see how we can perform this kind of action in ASP.NET Core.
First of all, let's add a new field to our Order.cs class:
